## Bicubic Patch, proving both the geometric winding (a transposed "P"
## culls under Sides 1 -- the point set is identical either way, so this
## is invisible under Sides 2 or Ka-only shading) and the per-vertex
## analytic normal (a backward getNormal() darkens under a directional
## light instead of disappearing). Control net in RISpec's bicubic order:
## sixteen points as four rows of four, u varying within a row, v across
## rows -- laid out here as row -> x, column -> y so the flat patch faces
## the camera.
Display "patch_bicubic.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 200 200 1
Projection "perspective" "fov" [45]
Clipping 0.5 50
Translate 0 0 5
WorldBegin
LightSource "ambientlight" 1 "intensity" [0.1]
LightSource "distantlight" 2 "intensity" [0.5] "lightcolor" [1 1 1]
	"from" [0 0 -5] "to" [0 0 5]
Sides 1
Surface "matte" "Ka" [0.2] "Kd" [0.7]
Patch "bicubic" "P" [
	-0.5 -0.5 0        -0.5 -0.166667 0        -0.5 0.166667 0        -0.5 0.5 0
	-0.166667 -0.5 0   -0.166667 -0.166667 0   -0.166667 0.166667 0   -0.166667 0.5 0
	0.166667 -0.5 0    0.166667 -0.166667 0    0.166667 0.166667 0    0.166667 0.5 0
	0.5 -0.5 0         0.5 -0.166667 0         0.5 0.166667 0         0.5 0.5 0
]
WorldEnd
